pocketmod: a ProTracker MOD player in one header, by rombankzero (MIT, see LICENSE).
https://github.com/rombankzero/pocketmod at commit 33ac2ba2f7c57aad0944a359e04bde5b2668470d (2018-06-14),
pocketmod.h with one change, marked "np2d" in _pocketmod_render_channel: the number of samples to write
is computed without a float-to-int overflow (UBSan, damaged modules). np2d builds it in src/modplay.c to play a game's audio/<id>.mod as its music.
Its interpolation can read up to 2 bytes past a sample's end (found by tests/mod_test.c under ASan with a damaged
module): modplay.c pads every loaded module with zeros instead of changing pocketmod.h.
